<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samaria</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sebaste</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Samaria was the capital of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-israel">Kingdom of Israel</a>, founded by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omri">Omri</a> in the early 9th century BCE on a hill in the central highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrians</a> took it in 722 BCE and deported much of the population. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-the-great">Herod the Great</a> rebuilt it as Sebaste. The name also came to refer to the surrounding region and its Samaritan people.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/samaria.jpg" alt="Samaria" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniel Ventura · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Views_from_Sebastia_18.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
